We have a number of sites that are using DECStation 5000/240s as servers 
running Ultrix 4.3 under enhanced security mode.  Our users log into these 
servers from X-Windows work stations and are very happy until their password 
expires.

We like to use the xdm process to manage the log-ons.  This allows us to 
tailor startup scripts and X-resources based on their X-server configuration.  
A couple of years ago I modified the xdm code from MIT to operate under Ultrix 
enhanced security.  

Unfortunately xdm does not manage the process of prompting 
a user for a new password when it expires. This wasn't a problem until we 
added some remote users.   Is anyone else using xdm under enhanced security or 
is there some other mechanism that I could use that would work equally as 
well?  Our users *have* to be able to change their password from their work 
station.  Any help would be appreciated.

