DEC OSF/1 does indeed have native realtime support.  This includes
such things as POSIX 1003.1b (previously 1003.4) support, preemptive
kernel POSIX threads, SMP, etc.

DECelx is actually called VxWorks for Alpha AXP, and is a toolkit for
developing applications for Alpha AXP and Motorola 68K targets (running
the VxWorks kernel).  Digital has ported the VxWorks kernel (from WRS) 
to 64 bits, added support for the Alpha AXP architecture, and provided 
several Board Support Packages (including an Alpha AXP VME board).

|>I prefer mail responses and will naturally summarize.

I have already responded by mail, this posting is just to clear up 
an public misconceptions about DEC OSF/1 and VxWorks (a.k.a. DECelx)

