The ZLX-E1 card is supported in OpenVMS AXP V6.1, for support
on V1.5 you need to install the Open3D layered product, which
includes the X11/Motif support.

All of the ZLX cards have 3D capabilities (the -E series are
primarily high-end 2D with low-end 3D capability).  To use the
3D capabilities (PEX, OpenGL, etc), you must install Open3D on
all versions of OpenVMS AXP.

2D (X11/Motif) support will be provided on the OpenVMS AXP
release that follows the availability of the option, but
"early" support will often be available through the Open3D
layered product.

BTW - the ZLX-E1 screams.  When measured on the DEC 3000-900 it
achieves the *highest* 2D x11perf numbers of *any* option on
the market.

