In article <772211021snz@trideuk.demon.co.uk> paul@trideuk.demon.co.uk (Paul Jolliffe) writes:

> CARD NUMBER
> 
> Unknown
> 
> +-----+   +----------+                            +------------------------+
> |.....|   |..........|     +-------------------+  |                        |
> |.....|   |..........|     | O | O | O | O | O |  | BIG RIBBON CABLE       |
> +-----+   +----------+     +-------------------+  +------------------------+
>   \_______   ______/         ^   ^                         ________
>           \_/                |   |                        _|      |_
>    GOES TO SEL/SLU         LIT   LIT                      \        /
>         MODULE           GREEN   RED                        \    /
>                                                               \/

  Presumably a MicroVAX II CPU board (M7606). This is status code 8, meaning
one of: A) User is being prompted to select a language, B) Informing the user
that the CPU is halted, or C) Indicating a failure. Since you get the console
prompt (>>>) I suspect it's B.

> M7196
> =====
> 
> +------------------------+      +-----------+     +------------------------+
> | BIG RIBBON CABLE       |      | O | O | O |     | BIG RIBBON CABLE       |
> +------------------------+      +-----------+     +------------------------+
>                                       ^
>                                       |
>                                  FLASHING RED

  TSV05 (1/2" magtape) controller. Center LED blinking means controller self-
tests are running.

> M7500
> =====
> 
>            +---------------+   +-----------+     +------------------------+
>            | O | O | O | O |   | O | O | O |     | BIG RIBBON CABLE       |
>            +---------------+   +-----------+     +------------------------+
>                  ^               ^
>                  |               |
>               RED LIT        GREEN LIT

  KMV1A-M Programmable Communications Controller. These lights don't match
my documentation, though.

> M3107
> =====
> 
> +------------------------+      +---+
> | BIG RIBBON CABLE       |      | O |
> +------------------------+      +---+
>                                   ^
>                                   |
>                                GREEN LIT

  DHQ11. It's happy.

> M7546
> =====
> 
> +---+   +--------------+
> | O |   | SMALL RIBBON |
> +---+   +--------------+
>   ^
>   |
> RED LIT

  TQK50. It has 2 LED's, though. Looks like it hasn't been initialized. A
"B MUA0" on the console should make both LED's go off and then maybe flash
if there's no tape in the drive (or no drive).

> M9405
> =====
> 
> +---+     +------------------------+
> | O |     | BIG RIBBON CABLE       |
> +---+     +------------------------+
>   ^
>   |
> GREEN
>  LIT

  Interconnect module. This looks like the wrong slot for it, though. It's
supposed to be in the top left slot of the bottom cabinet, with a M9404 in
the bottom left slot of the top cabinet.

> M7164
> =====
> +------------+ +-----------------+   +-------------------+ +------------------+
> |RIBBON CABLE| |RIBBON CABLE     |   | O | O | O | O | O | | RIBBON CABLE     |
> +------------+ +-----------------+   +-------------------+ +------------------+
>                                                    \  /
>                                                     \/
>                                                   BOTH LIT

