There are several UNIX utilities which will read/write ANSI labelled
tapes.  In fact there are programs to read and write IBM SL tapes,
ANSI SL tapes,  IBM CMS "Tapedump" tapes, VAX Backup tapes,
disk images of tapes, multi-volume tapes (several formats), etc.
There are programs for VMS and CMS to read
and write Unix Tar tapes.  All of these programs are available
on the net in standard archives. Most of them are contributions
to comp.sources.unix. Over the years I have collected these and every
other pd-Unix tape utility I have run across. Several of these
are in use here -- others are just taking up disk space.
I don't remember the exact path (I can post it later if necessary)
but many of these programs can be found in a single directory
on wuarchive (or its mirrors). A few can be found at other sites
also -- I recall that UCSB has several on its ftp server. Try running
an ARCHIE search on "tape".  You'll surely get a lot of junk,
but you may also find some gold.
