In article <771939926snz@trideuk.demon.co.uk>, paulj@trideuk.demon.co.uk (Paul Jolliffe) writes:
> The RA81 starts up O.K. and goes READY but the port A light does not light
> apart from that everything seems O.K.
> 
> Can anybody help ???

  The A port light won't come on until the drive is accessed by the host. You
should have a flat black rubberized cable (labeled BC27A) connecting the dis-
tribution panel at the bottom of the drive cabinet to the back of the CPU box.
There should be 4 matching connectors on the CPU box (2 in each of the panels)
and you can use any one of them. The distribution panel on the bottom of the
drive cabinet is labeled A and B - make sure you're in A, or press both of the
A and B buttons on the RA81 in (you *did* have the A button in before, right?).
You can't cheat and just use the cable off the drive to the CPU box - the dis-
tribution panel at the bottom of the drive box is a gender changer. You always
need an odd number of cables and an even number of distribution panels (cable
from controller to CPU panel, cable from CPU panel to drive panel, cable from
drive panel to drive).

  If that doesn't do it, the internal cables on the KDA50 controller may have
come loose - there are 4 red cables in webbing that connect the back of the
cabinet to the controller in the backplane, and it's hard to get it on proper-
ly and completely. There's also 2 cables connecting the 2 controller cards,
but it's less likely they're loose/off.

