		VMS CPU Model Summary (February 1993)
		-------------------------------------

The following table  summarises the whole known VAX and AXP model range by CPU
type, divided into processor families, and then by subtype (XCPU), giving
approximate chronological order. It gives the SID (containing the CPU type),
subtype (XCPU), ID, approximate power (relative to a VAX-11/780), main I/O bus
type (U=UNIBUS, M=MASSBUS, C=CI, Q=QBUS,  B=BI, D=DSSI, X=XMI, T=Turbochannel,
S=SCSI), model names, and nickname. 

Information is from publicly available sources such as DEC brochures and press
releases, together with the description of SYS$GETSYI in the VMS documentation,
and from $PRDEF, $VAXDEF, and $ALPHADEF in the system macro library. This is
supplemented with information from USENET group comp.os.vms. Current models are
marked by a leading `*'. 

This list is not an official publication of Laser-Scan - ask DEC if you want
confirmed figures! However, please let me know of any inaccuracies or ommisions.

