In article <2tn044$7li@news.belwue.de>, mab@calvin.ergo.iao.fhg.de (Matthias Bues) writes:
> What is special with a VAXStation 3100/M38 ? I got only 
> documentation for the Model 30. Looking at the config of my M38 I can find
> a 8-plane gfx option, 16megs of memory and two RZ23 disks. Is there 
> anything else special about it, such as a faster CPU ?

  The M38 has the exact same system board as a high-revision model 30. The
only difference is the clock crystal (66.6667Mhz instead of 44.4444), the
two boot/diagnostic PROMs, and a jumper. There's a cheat sheet going around
that shows how to convert a M30 to a M38 - you don't even need the PROMs,
although DEC will sell them to you. It's a rather hairy upgrade, though -
you can easily total your system board if you're not ultra-careful.

