In article <2to58e$171@network.ucsd.edu> ewa@cs.ucsd.edu (Eric Anderson) writes:
>I have an rz28 disk (2 GB or so) and I want it to spin up at power-on.
>Even my OSF/1 2.0 system doesn't know what an rz28 is, so I despair of
>using "rzdisk" on the Ultrix systems here.  Does anyone know if there
>is a jumper I can set?  (or, if some software tool can do this?)

OSF/1 2.0 *does* know an rz28. Both Ultrix and OSF/1 also know how to
spin up the drive when it's needed. In case you want to use the drive
somewhere else with broken SCSI (i.e. it doesn't know the standard
spinup command), put a jumper across pins 13-14 and it will spin up
on powerup.

