|>firmware, of course. 
|>... Or maybe somebody knows a drive existing in both SCSI and DSSI
|>variants, so just changing a ROM chip would solve it?

  If your intent is to simply try to connect a SCSI disk onto a DSSI,
  you should look into the HSD05 array controller.  The HSD05 allows
  you to hook up to seven SCSI devices off each available DSSI port.

  The HSD05 can fit inside a 3.5" StorageWorks brick and can thus mount
  directly inside a BA350 shelf, or it can be imbedded inside various
  DSSI VAX systems.

  Reverse engineering a DSSI bus is probably more work than most folks
  want to deal with.

