Our toshiba 3301 CDROM drives stopped working when we went to Ultrix
4.3a (Forcing up to use CAM). The problem is that PC CD-ROM drives use
a block size of 2048 bytes but Ultrix and OSF/1 need 512 byte block
size.

By looking at the cam_data.c file I found that there is an example
SONY cd-rom entry that issues a set up command to set the CD-Rom to
512 bytes/block when the device is opened. I copied this to create an
entry for a Toshiba cd-rom.

I have tested this on Ultrix 4.3a (Decsystem 5100) with a 3301 and
OSF/1 (Decstation 3000/400) with 3301 and 3401 ( I have been unable to
get an NEX 3Xi to work) .

Here is my /sys/data/cam_data.c entry. You will need to rebuild the
kernel after editing this file.

I am not sure if all the fields are correct for the Toshiba drive but
i have not had any problems to date.

/* Toshiba Cd-Rom */
{"TOSHIBA CD-ROM", 14, DEV_RRD42, (ALL_DTYPE_RODIRECT << DTYPE_SHFT) , 
  (struct pt_info *)ccmn_rrd40_sizes, 512, DEC_MAX_REC, NO_DENS_TAB,
  &sony_mode_sel, SZ_NO_FLAGS,
