Well, for those of you who've seen the same thing, here's the workaround 
that I came up with.  Not pretty, but it's better than dumping core:

int ret;

setupterm(0, 1, &ret);
if(ret != 1)
{
   printf("Your terminal type '%s' is not in the terminfo database!\n", 
      getenv("TERM"));
   exit(1);
}

