> I have a DEC Alpha 3000/600 Running OSF/1 1.3
> I'd like to have a different 'quoted text'
> marker in mailx (the default being a <TAB> space)
> The man pages indicate that using
> set indentprefix=string
> in .mailrc will accomplish this.  I tried and
> nothing happened.

I noticed this problem too in OSF/1 2.0, and did some digging.  Doing
a "strings" on the mailx program shows that while the other variables
listed in the man page are there (prompt, etc.), the string "indent"
is nowhere in the program.  This must mean that the DEC distribution
of mailx has non-matching program and man pages.

My solution:  I snagged the mail program from the FreeBSD distribution
that *DOES* correctly support the "indentprefix" variable.  It actually
looks like this is the version of mail that the DEC mailx is *supposed*
to be.  I had to fix one alignment problem in the code, and there's
still another less serious bug I haven't tracked down yet, but it is
certainly workable.  If people are interested I can put this up for
anonymous ftp somewhere....

