I believe that is just a new label for UCX.  I used UCX for about a week 
about 3 years ago and threw it out since it crashed the VAX every time it 
started.  I've never heard much good about it.  I am fairly sure but not 
certain it offers NFS client and server.

On the other hand, we just 2 weeks ago needed TCP/IP for a VAX, and I got
the TGV Multinet on a trial (easy to get 30 days free BTW).  It installed
without effort (and without reading anything but brief installation
instructions) and was up and running trivially, including NFS. 

I'm a novice to unix but a long time heavy VAX user.  I was extremely 
impressed by how easy it was to get it all up and running on the VAX.
Smoother than 95% of the Digital products in that regard (and the way DEC
is going closer to 100%).

I cannot give you a side by side comparison, but I would definitely want 
some awfully good reason to buy the DEC product given its long history of 
people's complaints and TGV's long history of happy comments.

