All right, lets see now (digging out my VS2000 tech manual)
what you really SHOULD use is a BCC08 console cable...

This is like the ordinary BCC05 printer cable, with the addition
that pin 8 and 9 are connected to each other.

When this is connected to the (9-pin) printer connector
the VS2000 will speak console on pins 2,3 and 7 like any serial port
at 9600 baud (I think) and ignore the video screen (for console purposes).
No jumper moves are necessary.

Hope this helps,
