When I got home, I checked the spec sheet;  It's not 1ft, it's 1m.

So the caculation goes something like:
20cm v 100 cm, use 1/r^2, factor by 4/100 ~= 14dB difference, giving
47dBA and 52dBA at 20cm.  Still  pretty quiet.  The DSP3210 is the same
thing as the RZ28 isn't it, which people are reporting as pretty quiet?
(DSP3210: 8 platters, 16 heads, 3042 tracks/surf, 5400rpm, formatted: 2.1GB).

(Also, please note that fans are sometimes pretty loud themselves, so
noise from disks in external cases is sometimes confused with the fan
noise;  this is one place where DECs "don't spin up until I say"
practice for SCSI drives is useful; you can get an idea of the
fan noise level before spinning up the disks to see which is
really causing the noise).



