dsr@lns598.tn.cornell.edu (Daniel S. Riley) writes:

>I don't have source to peruse, but the 'mount(1)' man page would seem
>to imply that it does do synchronous writes unless you mount with the
>'nosync' option (I certainly hope it works that way, as the default
>ought to conform to the NFS spec).

This is something else and doesn't affect NFS.  For UFS, synchronous writes
means that write() waits for I/O to complete.  The default is asynchronous
writes, but I believe we do a sync on close.  Also, any write that touches
the last byte of a 8K block will write that block.
