In article <1994Jun6.154629.260@sil.org>, titus@sil.org (Mike Titus) writes:

  >How can I set it so that the comma and period keys send comma and period
  >in both shifted and unshifted modes, like on an LK201? I like having
  >the <ALT> key available, too, so I haven't changed the keyboard setting
  >in Session Manager to LK201.

If you just want to do this in your DECterm windows, then you can enable
the "Comma Key Sends ,," option in the Keyboard Options dialog box (this
will also affect the period key).  If you want to do this in all windows,
you have to edit the keymap file, but this is fairly simple.  I'm assuming
you are using a US LK401 keyboard.  Change the following lines in the file
DECW$KEYMAP:US_LK401AA.DECW$KEYMAP:

E8      002C            003C            ! , <
ED      002E            003E            ! . >

to:

E8      002C            002C            ! , <
ED      002E            002E            ! . >

Actually, you may want make a copy of this file and place it in
DECW$SYSCOMMON:[SYS$KEYMAP.DECW.USER] instead of editing it in place in
DECW$SYSCOMMON:[SYS$KEYMAP.DECW.SYSTEM], and rename it to something like
US_LK401AA_COMMA_COMMA.DECW$KEYMAP.

Alfred

