>I don't think that anything done under the Options/keyboard
>menu actually affects the (or just my?) decterm settings -- is that
fair?

 To setup the keyboard so that it is using the correct keycodes,
 select OPTIONS from the SESSION MANAGER window, then select KEYBOARD
 and then select the appropriate keyboard type.

 To select between the < and , in *DECterm* select OPTIONS in the
 DECTERM window, then select Keyboard, and then select the appropriate
 value for "Comma key sends ,," or "Comma key sends ,<" this selection
 applies to *both* the comma key and the period key.

 To make it the DECterm default for *you* - simply save the settings.
 To make it the default for *everyone*, you would need to find the
 DECterm defaults .DAT file in DECW$SYSTEM_DEFAULTS

 The keymap files are layed out to follow the engravings, so by
 default - non DECterm windows will get ",," on a LK201 and ",<"
 on a LK401.  You can override this be either creating a XMODMAP
 script or by creating a new keymap file in DECW$KEYMAP with the
 change to the shifted values of the key, and then selecting that
 keymap file.


