>	Recently I got a DECstation 3100 with the RZ23 Hard drive in it.  
>I have little to no previous experience with DEC's and was wondering what 
>I need to make the DEC boot on the Drive.  The drive does not spin up 
>when I start the unit, this may be a bad drive or just something I have 
>to do.  I have taken the drive and put it on a PC with an adaptec 1542CF 
>controller and it has recognized the drive, but also did not spin it 
>up.   ANy help/Info would be greatly appreciated.  I am very new to this 
>unit and am looking for any info/manuals available.
>
>Alan Chook


These RZ23 drives are usually configured for expecting a Motor On command
to spin up. I did almost the same as you on a VAXstation 3100 (don't know
the differences between both). What I found out without documenation:
This machine has a switch on the back side which toggles between direct boot 
and entering the monitor firmware. It has a HELP cmd which shows the commands
available. Entering SHOW DEV will show all peripherals in the system (Disks,FDDs,Ethernet).
All devices will be checked; the disk should spin up now.
SHOW BOOT will show the device from which to boot. If this is the Ethernet,
you don't have a bootable disk in your machine (this was the fact with mine).
In this case you need to create a bootable disk somehow. 
If you can get some system software on CDROM: A usual SCSI CDROM (such
as a Toshiba 4101) should work with your machine; at least it does with
a VAXstation.


