(Vincent E. Kargatis) writes:
>Apologies if this is the wrong place to ask - please direct me to the proper
>forum if so.
>
>I'm trying to compile some software written for VAX on an Alpha, and one
>initial problem it has is not recognizing the FORTRAN underflow condition
>handler FOR$UNDERFLOW_HANDLER.  Is this nonexistent in Alpha FORTRAN?  Is there
>a substitute or easy fix?  

For some reason, the program is making an explicit reference to the
VAX Fortran RTL's underflow handler routine; why, I don't know.  The
correct way to do this is to compile with /CHECK=UNDERFLOW.  This
should work on OpenVMS AXP as well.  Direct use of FOR$UNDERFLOW_HANDLER
is undocumented and is not supported on AXP.

You'll have to figure out what the program is doing with the handler and
decide if removing the reference to it and compiling with
/CHECK=UNDERFLOW is sufficient.  Feel free to write me if you need
more assistance; send me the source of the routine which refers to
the handler so I can see what it is trying to do.

